base_view: solar_panel_large_public__electrical_performance
label: Electrical Performance
description: Electrical health and energy-yield measurements.
fields:
- solar_panel_large_public__electrical_performance.*
- solar_panel_large_public__panel_models.*
- solar_panel_large_public__plant_record.*
- solar_panel_large_public__plants.*
joins:
  solar_panel_large_public__plant_record:
    solar_panel_large_public__plants:
      solar_panel_large_public__panel_models: {}
ai_context: 'Reach related views through the declared joins on this topic instead of re-deriving relationships.

  Use the modeled business fields current_degradation_factor, effective_power_output, fill_factor_degradation, inverter_efficiency_loss, performance_ratio_metric, power_capacity_factor, severe_soiling_condition, soiling_loss_index, specific_yield_metric, system_power_loss_ratio, underperforming_asset, voltage_degradation_factor rather than reconstructing their formulas.

  Domain definitions for this topic:

  - Annual Degradation Rate (ADR): The annualized rate of performance loss, calculated as: $ADR = \frac{\text{Cumulative Degradation Pct}}{\text{Age in Years}}$.

  - Lifetime Revenue Loss Projection: A projection of future losses based on the Annual Degradation Rate (ADR). A simplified model is: $LRL = \text{ADR} \times \text{Annual Energy Production} \times \text{Energy Price} \times \text{Remaining Lifetime}$.

  - Chronic Downtime Asset: An asset is classified as having chronic downtime if its System Availability is below a critical threshold, for example, 95%.'
